-- title:
--   Ascent of regular local rings along regular sequences
-- statement:
--   The module establishes, for a Noetherian local ring $A$, that regularity descends from a quotient by a regular sequence back to $A$, the quotient being taken by `Ideal.ofList rs`, the ideal generated by the entries of a list $rs$.
--
--   Two preliminary facts are recorded for a commutative ring $A$: an element acting regularly on $A$ by scalar multiplication lies in `nonZeroDivisors A`; and if $rs$ satisfies `Sequence.IsRegular A rs` then `Ideal.ofList rs` is not the unit ideal, whence, over a local ring, every entry of $rs$ lies in `maximalIdeal A`. Next, the minimal number of generators `spanFinrank` of `Ideal.ofList rs` is bounded by `rs.length`, and consequently, for Noetherian local $A$ with $A/\mathrm{ofList}(rs)$ local, $\mu(\mathfrak m_A) \le \mu(\mathfrak m_{A/\mathrm{ofList}(rs)}) + |rs|$.
--
--   The main theorem `isRegularLocalRing_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_ofList` combines this generator count with the dimension identity $\dim(A/\mathrm{ofList}(rs)) + |rs| = \dim A$ for a regular sequence, and with the characterisation of regularity by $\mu(\mathfrak m) = \dim$, to conclude `IsRegularLocalRing A`. Variants assume instead that $rs$ is weakly regular with all entries in the maximal ideal, or transfer the conclusion along a surjection $f : A \to B$ with `RingHom.ker f = Ideal.ofList rs`. A second, independent route proves the same implication by induction on $|rs|$, at each step passing to $A/(x)$, identifying $A/(x)$ with `QuotSMulTop x A` so that the image sequence is again regular, and invoking the one-element ascent.
--
--   Two families of concrete checks follow: $[p]$ is a regular sequence in $\mathbb Z_p$ with $\mathbb Z_p/\mathrm{ofList}[p] \cong \mathbb Z/p$ regular, giving `IsRegularLocalRing ℤ_[p]` by either route together with the dimension jump; and over the dual numbers $\mathbb Q[\varepsilon]$ the singleton $[\varepsilon]$ fails to be regular, so that the analogous implication with regularity of the sequence weakened to mere membership in the maximal ideal is false.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** The notions used are Mathlib's: `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular` and `IsWeaklyRegular`, `Ideal.ofList`, `Submodule.spanFinrank` and `IsRegularLocalRing`. What is added here is the list-indexed ascent statement, built on the one-element case proved in the imported module `AlgebraicGeometry_RegularLocalRingQuotientNonZeroDivisorAscent`.
--
--   **Where it is used.** Recognising local rings as regular — in particular $\mathbb Z_p$, and quotients of power series rings by regular sequences — is the standard commutative-algebra input when deformation and Hecke rings are compared, as in the patching argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_AlgebraicGeometry_RegularLocalRingRegularSequenceAscent.lean

